  "body": "**Summary**\n\n`NonDimensionalizeByMetadata` divides the mesh coordinates by `L_ref` on each call. A dataset\nchain with two instances, one for interior `point_data` fields and one for boundary `cell_data`\nfields (inlet velocity, wall shear) read by a boundary model such as GLOBE, scales the geometry\nby `L_ref` twice. With `L_ref = 0.4 m` the coordinates were 2.5x too large in body units while\nthe fields were correct.\n\nThis adds `scale_geometry: bool = True`. The default is unchanged. A second instance sets\n`scale_geometry: false` and scales fields only. `inverse()` uses the same flag, so a chain of\ntwo instances inverts to the original geometry.\n\nA related bug in inference: `build_redim_field_types` kept only the last\n`NonDimensionalizeByMetadata` block's field map, so with two instances the interior predictions\nwould not have been re-dimensionalized. The maps are now merged.\n\n**Changes**\n- `src/nondim.py`: `scale_geometry` argument, applied in forward and inverse; docstring and\n  YAML example.\n- `src/infer.py`: merge the field maps of all `NonDimensionalizeByMetadata` blocks.\n- `tests/test_nondim.py` (new): default scales once; second instance does not rescale geometry;\n  inverse of both instances restores the input.\n- `tests/test_infer.py`: two-instance field-map merge.\n- `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n**Testing**\n`tests/test_nondim.py`, `tests/test_infer.py`, `tests/test_nested_targets.py`,\n`tests/test_synthetic_configs.py`: 70 passed. Pre-commit hooks pass. No dataset YAML in the\nrepo uses two instances, so existing recipes are unchanged.\n",
